## 🤖 ML-Based / Advanced Algorithm Ideas

### 11. Sequence Classification Model

**Description**: Use LSTM or Transformer model to classify sequences of draws and predict next likely numbers.
**Why**: Attempts to learn implicit temporal patterns (despite randomness).
**Python Tip**: Prepare input as sequences of past draws, output as binary vector for number presence.

---

### 12. XGBoost/RandomForest Based on Engineered Features

**Description**: Train a model per number with features like last seen, frequency in past 30 days, co-occurrence count, etc.
**Why**: Supervised learning approach for hit prediction.
**Python Tip**: Create per-number binary classification dataset.

---

### 13. AutoML Experimentation

**Description**: Feed historical draw dataset to a tool like PyCaret or Google AutoML.
**Why**: To identify hidden patterns without hand-tuning.
**Python Tip**: AutoML will perform feature selection, model choice, and scoring.

---

### 14. Reinforcement Learning Agent

**Description**: Build an agent that learns which combinations return best rewards (simulated wins) over time.
**Why**: Rewards based on historical win criteria.
**Python Tip**: Treat each draw as environment, reward = hits/prize.

---

### 15. Clustering-Based Generation

**Description**: Embed all past winning lines and apply clustering. Generate new lines within/around top clusters.
**Why**: Reproduce winning structures indirectly.
**Python Tip**: Use PCA or TSNE + KMeans.

---

Each of these algorithms can be wrapped in a strategy class and benchmarked using the simulation engine. Use versioning and logging to compare performance, hit rate, and ROI.
